    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "43eacbc40b778d5960a851e600bf25ef",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">(TF-IDF + LSA)</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A wave is only a convincing \"same object\" candidate if the <em>descriptions</em> resemble\neach other too. Only classical methods are used here: TF-IDF, truncated SVD (LSA)\nand cosine similarity.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For each wave we compute the mean pairwise cosine similarity of its reports and compare\nit to a <strong>null distribution</strong>: random sets of the same size drawn from the same state.\nThe z-score tells how much more alike the wave's reports are than chance.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
